Z||000019||falconhulk||11-05-2001||12:23 PM||||Exhaust wrap does not eat away at the pipe.  What it does do is hold moisture.  moisture causes rust.  Rust eats pipe.  In this application it will do so rather quickly as it will be fully exposed to the elements.||||reg||1
Z||000020||MinnGreenGT||11-05-2001||01:10 PM||||So... are you guys going to make a faux sidepipe?  I've always thought that might look cool.  I would suggest that you try driving your car for awhile without the muffler before you decide to go that route for sure... it's <B>loud</B> and sometimes annoying (that's why I'm going to build a bypass system).  Read this for some more exhaust info... check out an exhaust reducer instead of a small muffler- maybe use more than one?  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013191.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/013191.html</A> ||||reg||1
